# batches.jsonl holds the blinding keys (variant ids) of open review batches —
# committing it would unblind them. The warehouse JSONL itself IS committed.
**/batches.jsonl
data/embeddings/*.npy
data/embeddings/*.npz
data/embeddings/shards/
# Fresh-shard import drill, 2026-08-04 (loose end A11). Same policy as the pinned
# embeddings directory: the .ids.jsonl index and the manifest ARE committed, the
# vectors and the append-only write-ahead shards are not.
data/embeddings-fresh-15/*.npy
data/embeddings-fresh-15/*.npz
data/embeddings-fresh-15/shards/
oracle/**/.venv/
oracle/**/__pycache__/
# review-server runtime state (never committed)
data/review-server/server.pid
data/review-server/server.log
# Robustness perturbation cache: re-encoded and dithered copies of corpus covers.
# Same policy as the embeddings vectors — the SET FILES (pair-set-1.json,
# perturbation-set-1.json) ARE committed, the derived pixels are not. Every byte
# regenerates byte-identically from the corpus via
# `build-perturbation-set.ts --materialize` (verified 2026-08-04).
data/robustness/cache/
# The diff-viewer export (`check.ts --emit-diff-set`) is a convenience list of image paths
# regenerated on every run; the committed JSON report already carries the disagreeing trials.
data/robustness/reports/*.disagreements.txt
